      "actualCaller": "ElkGraphImporter.transformNode iterates original explicit ports, calls transformPort after node constraint normalization; transformPort copies properties, installs side/origin/owner, writes dimensions and position and registers identity, then calls initializePort with graph direction and optional PORT_ANCHOR. Caller spans are context only, not approval for their hierarchy/label/stream branches.",
      "reads": [
        "port.side",
        "port.pos",
        "port.size",
        "port.owner.size",
        "node PORT_CONSTRAINTS",
        "graph DIRECTION",
        "presence of PORT_BORDER_OFFSET",
        "optional explicit PORT_ANCHOR"
      ],
      "writes": [
        "inferred side and derived anchor through setSide",
        "PORT_BORDER_OFFSET only when absent and inferred side nonundefined with nonzero position",
        "PORT_RATIO_OR_POSITION for FIXED_RATIO",
        "port.anchor",
        "explicitlySuppliedPortAnchor when explicit anchor supplied"
      ],
      "branchFacts": [
        "UNDEFINED side is inferred only for constraints other than FREE/UNDEFINED; already selected side is retained.",
        "When both node dimensions are <=0 side inference returns UNDEFINED. For horizontal directions outside-x takes precedence; vertical directions use outside-y precedence. Otherwise diagonal percentage comparisons choose WEST/EAST then NORTH/SOUTH.",
        "One zero node dimension can produce JS Infinity/NaN during percentage inference. Preserve IEEE comparisons instead of adding positive-dimension restrictions or raising Python ZeroDivisionError.",
        "Border offsets are signed formulas for NORTH/EAST/SOUTH/WEST; presence of an explicit zero offset still blocks inference.",
        "FIXED_RATIO uses port top-left x/node width on NORTH/SOUTH and y/node height on EAST/WEST, guarded by dimension>0; default ratio0.",
        "Explicit anchor copies both coordinates and permanently marks it supplied; later setSide must preserve it. Default fixed-side anchors lie on the side boundary; FREE/UNDEFINED constraints use the center.",
        "Owner assignment removes then appends even for the same owner; reuse existing reviewed identity/order operation rather than sorting port IDs."
      ],
      "hostMappings": [
        "Property presence/default distinction reuses existing reviewed source mapping; no new Guava/GWT runtime implementation.",
        "LPort already has origin, pos, size, anchor and adjacency; add explicit supplied-anchor boolean default false in isolated graph copy.",
        "Use native IEEE-compatible division adapter for zero denominator, not a new bounded-domain guard."
      ],
      "notYetApproved": [
        "Full transformPort hierarchy/inside-connections/labels branches",
        "port comparator/order/index and graph direction transformations",
        "node-size context/constraint/alignment placement",
        "north/south dummy routing and long/in-layer edge handling",
        "public option resolution/import/export/admission expansion"
      ]
    }
  ],
